        {
          "name": "Step 1 - Interaction Network Retrieval",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://string-db.org/api/tsv/network?identifiers=820.ERS852554_01920&species=820&required_score=700&limit=20",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "string-db",
                "org"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tsv",
                "network"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "identifiers",
                  "value": "820.ERS852554_01920"
                },
                {
                  "key": "species",
                  "value": "820"
                },
                {
                  "key": "required_score",
                  "value": "700"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "### **network**\n\n**Use-case:** Retrieve the **full interaction network** for one or more proteins.\n\n```\nhttps://string-db.org/api/tsv/network\n    ?identifiers=STRING_ID\n    &species=TAXID\n    &required_score=700\n    &limit=20\n\n ```\n\n✔ Returns edges  \n✔ Includes combined scores + evidence channels  \n✔ You will use this for the “graph visualization”"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 1a -Best similarity hits between species",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://string-db.org/api/tsv/homology_best?identifiers=820.ERS852554_01920&species=820",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "string-db",
                "org"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tsv",
                "homology_best"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "identifiers",
                  "value": "820.ERS852554_01920"
                },
                {
                  "key": "species",
                  "value": "820"
                },
                {
                  "key": "species_b",
                  "value": "435590",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "## Retrieving best similarity hits between species\n\nSTRING internally uses the Smith–Waterman bit scores as a proxy for protein homology. The original scores are computed by [SIMILARITY MATRIX OF PROTEINS](http://cube.univie.ac.at/resources/simap) (SIMAP) project. Using this API you can retrieve these similarity scores between your input proteins and proteins in all of the STRING's organisms. Only the best hit per organism for each protein will be retrieved.\n\nThere are many organisms in STRING, so expect thousands hits for each protein, however you can filter the results to the list of organisms of interest by using 'species_b' parameter.\n\n#### Call:\n\n```\nhttps://string-db.org/api/[output-format]/homology_best?identifiers=[your_identifiers]\n\n ```\n\n#### Available output formats:\n\n| Format | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| tsv | tab separated values, with a header line |\n| tsv-no-header | tab separated values, without header line |\n| json | JSON format |\n| xml | XML format |\n\n#### Available parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| identifiers | required parameter for multiple items, e.g. DRD1_HUMAN DRD2_HUMAN |\n| species | NCBI/STRING taxon (e.g. 9606 for human, or STRG0AXXXXX see: [STRING organisms](https://string-db.org/cgi/input.pl?input_page_active_form=organisms)). |\n| species_b | a list of NCBI taxon identifiers seperated by \" \" (e.g. human, fly and yeast would be \"9606 7227 4932\" see: [STRING organisms](https://string-db.org/cgi/input.pl?input_page_active_form=organisms)). |\n| caller_identity | your identifier for us. |"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 2 - direct neighbours / interaction_partners",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://string-db.org/api/tsv/interaction_partners?identifiers=820.ERS852554_01920&species=820&limit=200",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
